{"name":"Yellow Polka Dot","hex":"#fcb867","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"polka","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lively dance originating in Bohemia.","The music for this dance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dance the polka."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polka"},{"term":"dot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Dass."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round spot.","A punctuation mark used to indicate the end of a sentence or an abbreviated part of a word; a full stop; a period."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polka dot","blocks":[{"text":"The polka dot, also written polkadot, and also called spot printed and spot print in the United Kingdom and pois (\"peas\") in France, is a pattern consisting of an array of large filled circles of the same size. Though the dots must be relatively large ones, and must be all the same size in any given print, different styles of polka dot prints may change the size of the dots or the distance between them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Polka_dots.svg/330px-Polka_dots.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polka_dot"},{"title":"Polka","blocks":[{"text":"Polka is a dance style and genre of dance music in 24 originating in nineteenth-century Bohemia, now part of the Czech Republic. Though generally associated with Czech and Central European culture, polka is popular throughout Europe and the Americas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/La_Polka.jpg/330px-La_Polka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polka"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg/500px-2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg/500px-2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail